F ToleranceAtLevel                     | AnalyticProjection.h | 98-101  | api,nonallocating,nonthrowing | ✔️ | The flattening tolerance one reduction level admits, in domain units. tolerance is wasteful at coarse levels and visibly polygonal at fine ones — and the coarse waste is the expensive one, since `20` §3 keeps the coarsest levels permanently resident and re-resolves them for every surface in the document. containment test at texel centres, so a chord deviating by less than one texel cannot move an answer; subdividing further buys positions no sample reads.
